        "content": "<p>alexcrichton closed <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/issues/14848\">issue #14848</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<h1>Cranelift x64: a <code>shuffle</code> whose mask reads one operand still depends on the other</h1>\n<h2>Summary</h2>\n<p>On x64, a <code>shuffle</code> gets a single <code>pshufb</code> only when both operands are the same<br>\nvalue (<code>shuffle a a</code>). If the operands differ but the mask only selects lanes from<br>\none of them (every index &lt; 16, or every index &gt;= 16), lowering falls through to:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>vpermi2b mask, a, b</code> when AVX512VL + AVX512VBMI are available, or</li>\n<li><code>pshufb a</code> + <code>pshufb b</code> (zeroing mask) + <code>por</code> otherwise.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Both read the operand the mask never selects. That costs instructions, and it<br>\nalso adds a false data dependency on that operand.</p>\n<p>Wasm producers emit this pattern. In <code>core::arch::wasm32::i8x16_shuffle::&lt;0, 4, 1,\n5, …&gt;(x, x)</code>, LLVM marks the second operand undefined, and the wasm backend fills<br>\nit with whatever local is handy. In the case below that local is the loop's<br>\naccumulator, so the shuffle waits on the previous iteration's add and the loop<br>\nruns serially. V8 lowers the same module to a single <code>pshufb</code>.</p>\n<h2>Reproducer</h2>\n<p>CLIF (<code>test compile precise-output</code>, <code>target x86_64 ssse3 has_avx512vl has_avx512vbmi</code>):</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Rust\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">function</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">%</span><span class=\"n\">shuffle_lhs_only</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">i8x16</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i8x16</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nc\">i8x16</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"n\">block0</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">v0</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nc\">i8x16</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v1</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nc\">i8x16</span><span class=\"p\">):</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"nc\">v2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">shuffle</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v0</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v1</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">4</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">6</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">7</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">8</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">12</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">9</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">13</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">10</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">14</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">11</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">15</span><span class=\"p\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v2</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Observed (<code>main</code> at dcfbea188d):</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Rust\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">movdqa</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">%</span><span class=\"n\">xmm0</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">%</span><span class=\"n\">xmm5</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">movdqu</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"o\">%</span><span class=\"n\">rip</span><span class=\"p\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">%</span><span class=\"n\">xmm0</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">movdqa</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">%</span><span class=\"n\">xmm5</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">%</span><span class=\"n\">xmm6</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">vpermi2b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">%</span><span class=\"n\">xmm1</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">%</span><span class=\"n\">xmm6</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">%</span><span class=\"n\">xmm0</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>With <code>target x86_64 sse41</code> it is two <code>pshufb</code>s and a <code>por</code>. Expected in both<br>\ncases: <code>pshufb (%rip), %xmm0</code>. The mirror case, every index &gt;= 16, behaves the<br>\nsame way with <code>v1</code> and <code>v0</code> swapped.</p>\n<p>Wasm loop showing the false dependency (<code>shuffle-false-dep.wat</code>, attached):</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"WebAssembly\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">loop</span> <span class=\"nv\">$l</span>\n  <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nb\">local.set</span> <span class=\"nv\">$v</span>\n    <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"err\">i</span><span class=\"mf\">8x16</span><span class=\"err\">.shuffle</span> <span class=\"mf\">0 4</span> <span class=\"mf\">1 5</span> <span class=\"mf\">2 6</span> <span class=\"mf\">3 7</span> <span class=\"mf\">8 12</span> <span class=\"mf\">9 13</span> <span class=\"mi\">10</span> <span class=\"mi\">14</span> <span class=\"mi\">11</span> <span class=\"mi\">15</span>\n      <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"err\">v</span><span class=\"mf\">128</span><span class=\"err\">.load</span> <span class=\"err\">…</span><span class=\"p\">)</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nb\">local.get</span> <span class=\"nv\">$acc</span><span class=\"p\">)))</span>          <span class=\"c1\">;; $acc is never selected</span>\n  <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nb\">local.set</span> <span class=\"nv\">$acc</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">i32</span><span class=\"err\">x</span><span class=\"mi\">4</span><span class=\"err\">.add</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nb\">local.get</span> <span class=\"nv\">$acc</span><span class=\"p\">)</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">i32</span><span class=\"err\">x</span><span class=\"mi\">4</span><span class=\"err\">.dot_i</span><span class=\"mi\">16</span><span class=\"err\">x</span><span class=\"mi\">8</span><span class=\"err\">_s</span> <span class=\"err\">…</span><span class=\"p\">)))</span>\n  <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nb\">br_if</span> <span class=\"nv\">$l</span> <span class=\"err\">…</span><span class=\"p\">))</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<h2>Impact</h2>\n<p><code>shuffle-false-dep.wat</code>, i7-1165G7 (has AVX512VBMI):</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>wasmtime</th>\n<th>time</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>49.0.3</td>\n<td>3.37 s (3.4 ns/iteration)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>with a single-operand lowering</td>\n<td>0.85 s (0.85 ns/iteration), 4.0× faster</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><code>n = 1_000_000_000</code>, <code>wasmtime run --invoke run shuffle-false-dep.wat 1000000000</code>,<br>\npinned to one core; two runs each agree to the hundredth of a second. The loop<br>\non 49.0.3:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Rust\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">vmovdqu</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"o\">%</span><span class=\"n\">rax</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">%</span><span class=\"n\">rcx</span><span class=\"p\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">%</span><span class=\"n\">xmm1</span>\n<span class=\"n\">subl</span><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"cp\">$</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">%</span><span class=\"n\">edx</span>\n<span class=\"n\">vmovdqu</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mh\">0x38</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"o\">%</span><span class=\"n\">rip</span><span class=\"p\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">%</span><span class=\"n\">xmm2</span>\n<span class=\"n\">vpermi2b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">%</span><span class=\"n\">xmm0</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">%</span><span class=\"n\">xmm1</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">%</span><span class=\"n\">xmm2</span><span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">%</span><span class=\"n\">xmm0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">is</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"cp\">$acc</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">never</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">selected</span>\n<span class=\"n\">vpmovsxbw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">%</span><span class=\"n\">xmm2</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">%</span><span class=\"n\">xmm1</span>\n<span class=\"n\">vpalignr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"cp\">$</span><span class=\"mi\">8</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">%</span><span class=\"n\">xmm2</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">%</span><span class=\"n\">xmm2</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">%</span><span class=\"n\">xmm2</span>\n<span class=\"n\">vpmovsxbw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">%</span><span class=\"n\">xmm2</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">%</span><span class=\"n\">xmm2</span>\n<span class=\"n\">vpmaddwd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">%</span><span class=\"n\">xmm2</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">%</span><span class=\"n\">xmm1</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">%</span><span class=\"n\">xmm1</span>\n<span class=\"n\">vpaddd</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">%</span><span class=\"n\">xmm1</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">%</span><span class=\"n\">xmm0</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">%</span><span class=\"n\">xmm0</span><span class=\"w\">       </span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"cp\">$acc</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>With <code>vpshufb 0x27(%rip), %xmm1, %xmm2</code> in place of the <code>vmovdqu 0x38(%rip)</code> /<br>\n<code>vpermi2b</code> pair, the shuffle no longer waits on the previous iteration's <code>vpaddd</code>.</p>\n<p>In a real int8 matrix-vector kernel (tract's <code>wasm_i32_4x1</code>, the inner loop of a<br>\ntransformer decoder's weight matmuls), patching only this operand in the module<br>\n(passing the loaded vector twice, so that <code>shuffle a a</code> matches) takes a<br>\n512×512 call from 56.7 µs to 27.2 µs on wasmtime 49.0.3: 2.1×, level with V8<br>\n(26 µs).</p>\n<h2>Where it comes from</h2>\n<p><code>cranelift/codegen/src/isa/x64/lower.isle</code>, <code>shuffle</code> rules: rule 3 is<br>\n<code>(shuffle _ a a …)</code>. Rules 2 and 1 (<code>vpermi2b</code>) and the <code>por</code> fallback take<br>\n<code>(shuffle _ a b …)</code> with no check on which operands the mask reads. Several<br>\nspecial cases already match \"lhs only\" or \"rhs only\" masks (<code>pshufd_lhs_imm</code> /<br>\n<code>pshufd_rhs_imm</code>, <code>pshuflw_*</code>, <code>pshufhw_*</code>), but no general byte shuffle does.<br>\nNeither the mid-end nor the wasm translator canonicalizes <code>shuffle a b</code> to<br>\n<code>shuffle a a</code>.</p>\n<h2>Related</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>#2531: shuffle optimizations needed. Closed once the common patterns got<br>\n  single-instruction lowerings; single-operand masks with distinct operands were<br>\n  not among them.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>#2930: added the <code>vpermi2b</code> lowering for shuffles of two different registers.<br>\n  It is the rule that now also catches these single-operand masks.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>#4772: port of the x64 shuffle lowering to ISLE (the rules above).</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>#5930, #5999: more <code>shuffle</code> specializations (<code>pshufd</code>/<code>pshuf{l,h}w</code> lhs/rhs,<br>\n<code>palignr</code>); they show the lhs/rhs-only pattern this needs.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>#6606: non-SSSE3 <code>pshufb</code> lowering (the <code>X86Pshufb</code> libcall).<br>\n</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>",
